`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Plugin sharing to groups allows Admins to override a plugin's org-wide availability for specific groups, further scoping plugin access — e.g. make a plugin available only to the Legal group, or auto-install it for Engineering while keeping it hidden from everyone else."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Governance posture does not currently control Connector access. Connectors are org-wide on/off today and you can't scope them per team. RBAC only governs capability access (Cowork, Code, etc.), not skill sharing."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:(0,n.jsxs)(r.strong,{children:["For how admins distribute skills and plugins (",(0,n.jsxs)(r.strong,{children:["admin-provisioned skills, group-scoped plugins, GitHub-synced marketplace), see ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13119606-provision-and-manage-skills-for-your-organization",children:"Provision and manage skills for your org"}),", ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13837433-manage-cowork-plugins-for-your-organization",children:"Managing Cowork plugins,"})," and ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13837433-manage-claude-cowork-plugins-for-your-organization#h_ac08ca5f63",children:"Customize plugin access by group"})]}),"."]})}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h2,{id:"3-champion-model",children:"3. Champion model"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Champions are enthusiastic adopters who can help drive peer adoption across their teams. They will be participants in your pilot if you run one, and play a key role in your Cowork rollout. Champions are the people who will test workflows, demo at workshops, maintain plugins, and drive adoption within their departments."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"who-makes-a-good-champion",children:"Who makes a good champion:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"A power user who is already getting value from AI tools - whether Claude or otherwise"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Willing to build and experiment for their teams"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Trusted by admins to help gather departmental feedback and surface blockers"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"how-to-find-champions",children:"How to find champions:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Usage analytics are a great signal for discovering champions. Anthropic provides per-user activity data which will help uncover power users early on."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Ask function leads to nominate"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Target ratio 1 champion per 25–50 users"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Mix technical and non-technical users across different departments"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Include enthusiasts and sceptics; an all-enthusiastic pilot gives false positives"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"what-to-give-champions",children:"What to give champions:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Permission to create Skills and consider turning on peer-to-peer Skill sharing for pilot group"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"A 30-minute orientation on skills, plugins, and the governance model you're using"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"A channel (Slack channel, Teams group) where champions across departments can share what's working"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Access to Anthropic's pre-built plugins as starting points"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Recognition for their contributions to the rollout"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"what-to-expect-from-champions",children:"What to expect from champions:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Build 2–3 starter skills for their team"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Help their teams audit workflows and generate use case ideas"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Run a skills workshop for their team"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Own and maintain their department's plugins; identify the need for sub-team plugins (ex. Marketing vs. Demand Gen)"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Surface what's working and what's not in the champions channel"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Do a quarterly curation review of their department's skills"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h2,{id:"4-rollout-phases",children:"4. Rollout phases"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"The organizations that see the fastest, deepest value invest in readiness, curate first experiences, and govern deliberately by following these five principles."}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Executive sponsorship"}),": Visible and sustained — not just a kickoff email."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Curated first experiences"}),": Guide users to high-value use cases, not blind experimentation."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Connectors enabled early"}),": The aha moment arrives faster when Cowork reaches existing tools."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Champion network first"}),": Every team needs someone who can demo, troubleshoot, and evangelize."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Governance defined upfront"}),": Connector approval, skill creation, and access policies from Day 1."]}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:["Here's what a typical Cowork rollout looks like. Adapt the pace to your org. Note that the phases below assume Setup and Configuration steps from the ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"/tutorials/claude-cowork-enterprise-administrator-guide",children:"Cowork Enterprise Admin Guide"})," are complete."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"phase-1-pilot",children:"Phase 1: Pilot"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Goal:"})," Validate your configuration and produce the first proof points with a small group of champions."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Admins and AI transformation teams own:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Recruit 1–2 champions per pilot department. Follow criteria in Section 3."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Enable initial connectors org-wide; sequence security review by risk tier (read-only first is common)"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Set initial governance posture for the pilot group based on strategy for skill and plugin sharing across your org"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Define 2–3 success metrics upfront and stand up feedback loops (pulse survey, dashboard review, escalation paths for feedback)"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Announce launch, initial connectors and enablement opportunities to the pilot group"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Champions own:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Install and try Anthropic's pre-built function plugins for their department"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Build 2–3 starter skills for their own work"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Report what's working / blocked in the champions channel"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Exit when ready:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:">70% weekly active users by week 4"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Each pilot department has multiple repeatable use cases validated and documented"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Champions are willing and briefed to run a workshop for their teams"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"What changes between pilot and broad rollout is usually the governance posture, new connectors cleared by security, and new departments onboarding with their own champions."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"phase-2-expansion",children:"Phase 2: Expansion"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Goal:"})," Turn pilot proof points into department-level adoption — the skill flywheel starts here."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Admins and AI transformation teams own:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Open access to the next wave of departments; onboard their champions"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Clear the next tier of connectors through security"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Revisit governance posture with pilot evidence (most orgs loosen here)"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Stand up self-service resources and a tiered support path (champion → program team → Anthropic)"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Watch spend patterns and adjust controls"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Champions own:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Run a skills workshop for their department (format → Section 5)"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Surface team-built skills; promote the best into the department plugin"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Share wins cross-department in the champions channel"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Exit when:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Every onboarded department has a maintained plugin with a named owner"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Workshop run in each department; majority of attendees built or adopted a skill"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Connector and governance requests are flowing through a defined process"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"phase-3-scale-and-monitor",children:"Phase 3: Scale and Monitor"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Goal:"})," Reach remaining departments and shift from launch mode to operating rhythm."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Admins and AI transformation teams own:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Roll the workshop motion to remaining departments"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Establish cadences: monthly champion check-in, quarterly governance review"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Stand up (or formalize) an AI Enablement CoE to own the skill library and advanced capabilities"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Move measurement from activity (WAU, sessions) to outcomes (time saved, use-case ROI); report quarterly"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Champions own:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Quarterly curation: surface the best skills from their teams, promote winners to plugins, archive stale skills, merge duplicates"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Onboard replacement champions as people rotate"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Building plugins and skills enablement into new-hire onboarding"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"You're in steady state when:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Every major department has an owned plugin and an active champion"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"New skills are entering the library faster from champions than from the program team"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.li,{children:"Quarterly ROI reporting is running based on business value, not just time-save"}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"The habit worth keeping past this rollout is reassignment. Every quarter, and every time a champion moves teams, ask who owns each plugin and each scheduled task now, and move that ownership on purpose. Widen what Claude runs on its own where the output has earned it; pull a task back to a person where it hasn't. The split you drew at pilot is a starting point you'll keep redrawing as the evidence comes in."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h4,{children:"Pitfalls to avoid:"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Launch ≠ enablement."})," IT flipping the switch and sending an email isn't a rollout.Treat a Cowork rollout as a program requiring change management."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"First-impression failure."})," Unguided experimentation underwhelms — curate starter use cases per role and have champions lead first sessions."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"The chat trap."})," Users default to short prompts with no connectors. Enablement must demo delegation side-by-side with chat. Push users to authenticate connectors when they get provisioned."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Treating config as permanent."})," Plan to revisit connectors and posture with usage evidence; a working proof point de-risks the next approval better than another security review."]}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Only measuring time-saved or login counts."})," Consider what ROI on Claude Cowork means for your business. Define outcome-based measures including net new work completed and qualitative feedback on use cases in addition to productivity measurement."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h2,{id:"5-enablement-methods",children:"5. Enablement methods"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:["Cowork training should be hands-on-keyboard when possible — the value shows up in ",(0,n.jsx)(r.em,{children:"doing"}),', not watching. But "training" is really three different jobs depending on where a user is in their journey. Reference Anthropics researched-backed ',(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"/tutorials/getting-good-at-claude-a-research-backed-curriculum",children:"AI Fluency principles"})," when designing enablement for your teams."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Enablement follows a natural progression: users start by completing a single task with a connector, then build competence with skills and plugins, then reach the point where Claude Cowork runs workflows for them automatically."}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h3,{id:"phase-1-activation-first-prompt-to-first-skill",children:"Phase 1: Activation (first prompt to first skill)"}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Get every user from zero to their first successful task with a connector."}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.ul,{children:[`
