`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Get everyone one scheduled task"}),". Once a user has a daily pipeline digest or weekly report landing automatically, Claude Cowork comes to them. Run this one yourself before you ask champions to teach it. In Cowork, ask in chat:"]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(i,{children:(0,n.jsx)(r.p,{children:"Every weekday at 8am, pull our open pipeline from the connected CRM, summarize the deals that changed stage yesterday, and post the digest to our team channel."})}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:["A scheduled task runs with the same access as any other Cowork session, so whatever it produces lands in your real tools. Before rolling the habit out, check the result the way you'd check a new hire's first report: open the channel after the first run and confirm the digest is there, covers yesterday's changes, and reads the way your team expects. A task that runs on time but posts the wrong summary is one your team will quietly stop trusting. See ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13854387-schedule-recurring-tasks-in-claude-cowork",children:"Scheduled tasks"}),"."]}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.li,{children:[`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Embed in existing rituals"}),". The standard for a weekly pipeline review becomes the Claude Cowork-generated digest. The standard for a monthly board deck becomes a Claude Cowork-assembled first draft. Attach Claude Cowork to existing working rhythms."]}),`
`]}),`
`]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Bake into new-hire onboarding"}),". Include Cowork in Day-1 checklist: install the desktop app, authenticate 3 connectors, install the department plugin, run its flagship skill. See ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/10065433-installing-claude-desktop",children:"Installing Claude Desktop"}),"."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsx)(r.h2,{id:"6-faq",children:"6. FAQ"}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Can I control which connectors specific users see?"})," No. Currently, you can only enable connectors org-wide."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"If I enable a connector, does Claude automatically access everyone's data?"})," No. Connectors use a two-gate model: an admin enables the connector org-wide, then each user individually OAuths to link their own account. Claude can only access data within that user's existing permissions."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Can users share skills that include API keys or credentials?"})," Skills should never contain credentials. If a skill needs authenticated access, it should use a connector. Include this in your champion training and skill-vetting process. We recommend creating a skill-audit skill that runs standard checks before approving skills for org-wide distribution or inclusion in plugins."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"How do I prevent people from creating duplicate or low-quality skills?"})," Namespace by department, run quarterly curation reviews, and use the champion model. The guided-creation posture is the best balance for most teams — people can create freely, but promotion to org level goes through a review."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"How do plugins sync with version control?"})," Plugins support GitHub sync. Connect a private GitHub repo as a plugin marketplace. Changes merge through your normal PR process and auto-sync to users. See ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/13837433",children:"Managing Cowork plugins"})," for repo structure details."]}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"What's the difference between a skill and a scheduled task?"}),' A skill runs when someone triggers it. A scheduled task is a saved prompt that Claude runs automatically on a schedule, with the same access as any other Cowork session. Users set one up by giving a prompt and picking a schedule in the Cowork UI, or by asking in chat. A natural-language request like "every day at 6am" is enough to create one, and most scheduled tasks get created that way. Scheduled tasks are a Cowork-only feature. Common use: a daily pipeline digest that runs every morning at 8am and posts to Slack.']}),`
`,(0,n.jsxs)(r.p,{children:[(0,n.jsx)(r.strong,{children:"Where do I go for help with desktop app installation or connector setup?"})," See the ",(0,n.jsx)(r.a,{href:"/tutorials/claude-cowork-enterprise-administrator-guide",children:"Claude Cowork Enterprise Admin Guide"}),", which covers desktop app deployment, connector configuration, and org architecture setup."]}),`
